Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Read the inode of the file a lock holds

A lock taken on a path can hold a file that the path no longer names: the file
was removed or replaced while the lock waited. To tell, the inode of the lock's
file is compared with the inode of the path. tbox keeps the file of a lock
private, so tb_filelock_file exposes it, and io.filelock_inode returns the inode
of its descriptor with fstat, or nil where a file has no inode (Windows).
_filelock:inode is the Lua side of it.

Self-review: crutches left

Changes-build-output: no

